## Startup sequence

```rust
#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    // 1. initialize structured logging (RUST_LOG controls verbosity)
    tracing_subscriber::fmt()
        .with_env_filter(...).init();

    // 2. open + create SQLite pool
    let pool = db::init_pool("sqlite://movies.db?mode=rwc").await?;
    // 3. run embedded SQL migrations
    db::run_migrations(&pool).await?;
    // 4. seed mock movies on first run
    mock_data::seed_if_empty(&pool).await?;

    // 5. assemble router, hand it the pool as shared state
    let app = build_router(pool);
    // 6. bind + serve
    let listener = tokio::net::TcpListener::bind(addr).await?;
    axum::serve(listener, app).await?;
    Ok(())
}
```

Four async calls, each `?`-propagating errors via `anyhow::Result`. If any fails, the program exits with a non-zero code before serving a single request.

